{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Forty-two cubes with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm edges are glued together to form a solid rectangular block. If the perimeter of the base of the block is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm, then the height, in cm, is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12af7011887eb367c0281509d793fc14165833ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{7}{3} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"337\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/inde